{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1377424-can-prometheans-especially-galateids-get-pregnant-or-get-someone-pregnant","id":1377424,"title":"Can Prometheans (especially Galateids) get pregnant or get someone pregnant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-30T18:32:39-07:00","id":1377424,"title":"Can Prometheans (especially Galateids) get pregnant or get someone pregnant?","content":"Is there an Alchemical procedure that would allow a Promethean to do this?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure the answer is no, but I don\u2019t know much about the game, so I thought I\u2019d ask.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1869\" data-vbnamecard=\"1869\">moonwolf8</a> gave me a really good idea. What if when Lancelot sleeps with Guinevere\u2019s cousin Elaine and gets her pregnant (this is before he and Guinevere go all the way for real), he\u2019s really sleeping with a Galateid disguised as Guinevere? Just wondering if it would work mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T19:29:22-07:00","id":1377438,"title":"","content":"In the 1e supplement <b>Magnum Opus</b>, there was a section on what were called Scions: progeny of human/Promethean matings. It's been a while since I've read the section; but from what I recall, the answer given was \u201cno, Prometheans can't bear or sire children \u2014 unless they can.\u201d No special Alchemical procedure was needed; just a fervent desire to have kids, not unlike <b>Saturnine Night</b> would subsequently reveal that the let interesting in a mortal creating a Promethean was a desperation to create life. If conception is successful, the resulting child is born immune to the effects of Disquiet. <br /> <br /> In 2e terms, I'd phrase this as \u201cconception is possible if the Promethean participant has a suitable Milestone; and conception has the further effect of resolving that Milestone\u201d. And since the nature of said Milestone involves procreation, it also counts as satisfying one of those key Milestones that must be satisfied before a Promethean can attain the New Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T19:33:56-07:00","id":1377441,"title":"","content":"Perfect! That totally works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T15:41:05-07:00","id":1379530,"title":"","content":"Depends on the edition, but the short answer for both editions is yes, but it\u2019s extremely difficult to the point of almost being impossible. Like Dataweaver said, if the Promethean is suitably close to completing the Great Work the odds of having a child would be higher than it ever normally would be.. but still incredibly rare.<br /> <br /> But for a Prommie straight off the slab.. yeah unless they were quirky like an Extempore they could have as much as sex as they could possibly want and nothing should come of it in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}